    "doi": "https://doi.org/10.3189/172756400781819996",
    "abstract": "Abstract Measurements of summer and winter mass balances have been carried out over the past 53 years on Storglaci\u00e4ren, northern Sweden. Repeated surveys of the glacier have resulted in several maps of surface topography as well as a map of the bed topography A new time-dependent ice flow model allows us to compare the observed surface evolution of the glacier with that computed by the model using measured mass-balance maps as input. The computed volume change compares well with the measured change: the model replicates the distribution of surface elevation to within \u00b110 m over 30 years of integration. On the model side, these deviations can be attributed to the low-resolution discretization of the model domain as well as to the limited accuracy of the ice rheology and omitted basal sliding. On the other hand, the uncertainties of the topography and mass-balance maps match the model uncertainties. In this sense, the experiments are a validation of both model and observations.",
    "field": "Glacier dynamics modeling",
    "problem": "This paper addresses the challenge of accurately modeling glacier evolution by validating a time-dependent ice-flow model's ability to replicate observed 30-year changes in a glacier's geometry when forced with detailed, measured mass-balance maps, thereby testing the accuracy of both the model and the observational data.",
    "method": "This study proposes a method to simulate glacier evolution by forcing a three-dimensional, time-dependent ice-flow model with measured mass-balance maps, validating the computed changes in surface elevation and volume against decades of repeated topographic surveys of the glacier.",
    "task": "The task is to validate a time-dependent ice-flow model by forcing it with measured mass-balance data for Storglaci\u00e4ren and comparing the model's computed glacier surface evolution with observed historical changes in topography between 1959 and 1990.",
    "model": [
        "GCM"
    ],
